  "turn": 1,
  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in your account ACC-1005:\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Type:** Card payment, outgoing, status settled\n\nYour account also shows **TX-0402**, another EUR 240.00 card payment to TechMart Online, dated 2026-07-14 and also settled. I mention it because two identical payments to the same merchant can matter if one was unintended.\n\nBased on the dispute reason codes available to me, these could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** The same purchase was charged more than once. TX-0401 and TX-0402 may fit this if you only intended to pay once.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorize the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** Your card details were used without your permission in an online transaction. TechMart Online is an online merchant, so this may be relevant.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid, but the item was never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nI have not opened any dispute. Tell me what happened with this payment, and I will check whether a dispute is eligible before doing anything. Opening one is irreversible, so I will confirm with you first.",
